10) = 3. So neither finished corner was recognised as a corner.\n\n**Repair:** test each frame arm at distances 2 and 3 from the corner instead of 1 and 2. A decoration reaches at most one cell along an arm, so the cells further out are still bare 0.\n\n- Pair 2, corner at the 1s, (3,5): (3,7), (3,8), (5,5) and (6,5) are all 0, so it is now detected.\n- Corners in pairs 1 and 3, and corners cut off by the grid edge: their arms are long enough on the visible side, so detection is unchanged there.\n\n**Expected result on pair 2.** With the template found (the ring of 1s, depth D = 1), these corners now get stamps: the 4 at (4,10), the 6 at (8,6), and the 2, 7, 3 and 4 inside the bottom frame. That is exactly the set of changes shown in the expected output.\n\n**Test input.** I expect the same behaviour. The 2-shape is detected because its arms 2–3 cells out are plain 0. It is then stamped at 4, 1, 6, 8 and 5.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    def get(y, x):\n        if 0 <= y < H and 0 <= x < W:\n            return g[y, x]\n        return -1\n\n    # frame corners: perpendicular arms (checked 2-3 cells out, since\n    # decorations may cover the first arm cell) are 0, diagonal not 0\n    corners = []\n    for y in range(H):\n        for x in range(W):\n            for dy in (1, -1):\n                for dx in (1, -1):\n                    if (get(y+2*dy, x) == 0 and get(y+3*dy, x) == 0 and\n                            get(y, x+2*dx) == 0 and get(y, x+3*dx) == 0 and\n                            get(y+dy, x+dx) not in (0, -1)):\n                        corners.append((y, x, dy, dx))\n\n    # template: the corner with the most same-coloured cells in its local window\n    best = None\n    for (y, x, dy, dx) in corners:\n        for d in (1, 2, 3):\n            c = get(y+d*dy, x+d*dx)\n            if c in (0, -1) or c == bg:\n                continue\n            cells = []\n            for u in range(-2, 4):\n                for v in range(-2, 4):\n                    if get(y+u*dy, x+v*dx) == c:\n                        cells.append((u, v))\n            if best is None or len(cells) > len(best[0]):\n                best = (cells, (y, x))\n            break\n    if best is None:\n        emit(out, \"No template corner found; grid unchanged.\")\n        return out\n    tmpl, tcorner = best\n    D = max(d for d in range(0, 4) if (d, d) in tmpl)\n\n    emit(out, \"Identified the already-decorated corner as the template.\")\n    for (y, x, dy, dx) in corners:\n        if (y, x) == tcorner:\n            continue\n        c = get(y+D*dy, x+D*dx)\n        if c in (0, -1) or c == bg:\n            continue\n        # skip corners that are already fully decorated\n        if all(get(y+u*dy, x+v*dx) in (c, -1) for (u, v) in tmpl):\n            continue\n        for (u, v) in tmpl:\n            yy, xx = y+u*dy, x+v*dx\n            if 0 <= yy < H and 0 <= xx < W:\n                out[yy, xx] = c\n        emit(out, f\"Stamped the mirrored corner template in colour {c} at corner ({y},{x}).\")\n    emit(out, \"All marked corners decorated.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"rigid":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamped the mirrored corner template in colour 3 at corner (3,3)."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamped the mirrored corner template in colour 4 at corner (10,3)."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamped the mirrored corner template in colour 2 at corner (10,10)."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Expected result on pair 2.** With the template found (the ring of 1s, depth D = 1), these corners now get stamps: the 4 at (4,10), the 6 at (8,6), and the 2, 7, 3 and 4 inside the bottom frame."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"It is then stamped at 4, 1, 6, 8 and 5."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Identified the already-decorated corner as the template."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"8e379c34862a400bf358b4249e8b50437f55b96dcfe76528999a1106737c2062","task_sha256":"3a38ec2ea5ea2ef37d9491a0f0ce527a2768833d90964aed88a5f23dcc872b5f","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
